WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
Freeze an oscillating particle, mid-swing.

2
00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.960
You know its amplitude and its period.

3
00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:08.250
You can see exactly where it is.

4
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.590
What you don't know is the time.

5
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.700
No clock, and no idea when it started.

6
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:18.920
From its position, without the time,
can you work out how fast it is moving?

7
00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:23.440
In this mission, you'll use a phase angle
to say exactly where in its cycle an

8
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.200
oscillator starts.

9
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.170
Then you'll write its velocity
as a function of time,

10
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.600
and set it beside its displacement.

11
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:34.560
Your mission: find out whether
its position tells you the speed,

12
00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.790
and explain why.
